## Key Migration Points

### 1. Remove WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter
- No longer extend `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter`
- Create `SecurityFilterChain` bean instead
- Use lambda DSL for configuration

### 2. Update Method Security Annotation
```java
// Old
@EnableGlobalMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true, securedEnabled = true)

// New
@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true, securedEnabled = true)
```

### 3. Replace antMatchers with requestMatchers
```java
// Old
.antMatchers("/api/public/**").permitAll()
.antMatchers(HttpMethod.POST, "/api/users").permitAll()

// New
.requestMatchers("/api/public/**").permitAll()
.requestMatchers(HttpMethod.POST, "/api/users").permitAll()
```

### 4. Use Lambda DSL
Spring Security 6 prefers lambda-based configuration:
```java
// Old style (still works but deprecated)
http
    .csrf().disable()
    .authorizeRequests()
        .antMatchers("/public/**").permitAll();

// New style (preferred)
http
    .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
    .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
        .requestMatchers("/public/**").permitAll()
    );
```

### 5. AuthenticationManager Bean
```java
// Inject AuthenticationConfiguration and get the manager
@Bean
public AuthenticationManager authenticationManager(
        AuthenticationConfiguration authConfig) throws Exception {
    return authConfig.getAuthenticationManager();
}
```

